    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1343">

                <pb facs="1316" n="1306" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="32" xml:id="d1343-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-19T17:00:00+08:00">August 19, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 19—5:43 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3341. Attempted bombing customs lighthouse tenders August 18, 3 p.m. (ConGentel
                    3311, August 18<anchor n="33" xml:id="d1343-f2"/>), illustrates essentiality
                    prompt assurances responsible authorities Canton and Taipei safe conduct,
                    noninterference proposed call <hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi> September 17
                    if withdrawal Americans on that vessel to succeed. Safe conduct given by Chinese
                    Nationalist Government Canton probably insufficient protect evacuation vessels
                    from bold daylight aerial attacks based on Taiwan unless Generalissimo notified
                    and his personal assurance obtained.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated OffEmb Canton 1029.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
